1. Definitions

  “Software” means the source code, binaries, documentation and assets
  in this repository, excluding third-party dependencies, which remain
  under their own licences.

  “Licensor” means K0uzia, the copyright holder.

  “You” means any individual or entity using the Software.

  “Internal Use” means use for your own purposes or those of your
  organisation, including professional or for-profit operations,
  provided the Software is not supplied to third parties as a product
  or service.

  “Commercial Redistribution” means sale, paid licensing, rental,
  sublicensing, OEM, white-labelling, or making the Software (or a
  substantially similar product) available to third parties for a fee
  or as a commercial offering, including as SaaS.

2. Grant

  Subject to this licence, the Licensor grants you a worldwide,
  non-exclusive, non-transferable, royalty-free, revocable right to:

  a) use, copy and modify the Software;
  b) deploy it for Internal Use;
  c) study how it works.

3. Restrictions

  Without prior written permission from the Licensor, you may not:

  a) engage in Commercial Redistribution;
  b) sell the Software, a fork, a modified version, or a substantially
     similar product;
  c) offer the Software as a paid service or competing offering;
  d) remove or alter copyright and licence notices.

  A separate commercial licence may be obtained from the Licensor.

4. Non-commercial distribution

  You may redistribute the Software, modified or not, on a
  non-commercial basis, provided that:

  a) this licence accompanies it, unaltered;
  b) copyright notices are preserved;
  c) substantial modifications are documented.

5. Contributions

  Contributions submitted to the repository are licensed to the
  Licensor under these terms, royalty-free, for the term of copyright.
  You warrant that you have the rights required to grant this licence.

6. Trademarks

  No rights are granted to the Licensor’s names, logos or trademarks,
  including “Tracebaie” and “K0uzia”, other than fair attribution.

7. Disclaimer

  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED “AS IS”, WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND,
  EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A
  PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NON-INFRINGEMENT.

8. Limitation of liability

  IN NO EVENT SHALL THE LICENSOR BE LIABLE FOR ANY DIRECT, INDIRECT,
  INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL OR CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES ARISING FROM USE OF THE
  SOFTWARE, TO THE EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW.

9. Termination

  Any breach automatically terminates your rights. Sections 6, 7, 8
  and 10 survive termination. Upon termination you must cease use and
  destroy copies in your possession, unless legally required otherwise.

10. Governing law

  This licence is governed by French law. Disputes are submitted to
  the competent courts of France, subject to mandatory consumer
  protection rules.

11. Contact

  Commercial licensing: https://github.com/K0uzia
